    <span>🔹</span> Plant Kingdom Classification
  </h3><h4 style="border-left: 3px solid var(--info); padding-left: 8px; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600;">High-Yield Formulas & Facts</h4><ul style="margin-left: 20px; list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary);"><li style="margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.6;"><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Thallophyta:</strong> Algae (no roots/stems/leaves)</li><li style="margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.6;"><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Bryophyta:</strong> Amphibians of plant kingdom (Funaria/Moss)</li><li style="margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.6;"><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Pteridophyta:</strong> First vascular plants (Ferns/Marsilea)</li><li style="margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.6;"><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Gymnosperms:</strong> Naked seeds (Pinus/Cycas)</li><li style="margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.6;"><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Angiosperms:</strong> Enclosed seeds, flowers, Monocots & Dicots</li></ul>
</div>`;

